course: dictionary
lesson: 3190
title: Words that warn us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To endanger something means to put it in danger, so that harm is likely. It can be a person, an animal, or a plant. «Running by the pool can endanger others.» The running makes it likely that someone gets hurt.
explain: Endanger is a verb, so its form changes: endangers, endangered, endangering. In «endangered species», the word means animals or plants that might die out. Ask yourself: what could be lost or harmed? If the answer is an animal or plant, the word probably means it might die out.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Pollution endangers wildlife» tells you that pollution makes animals and plants more likely to be lost. Test your meaning in the sentence: "Pollution puts wildlife in danger" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Scientists use this word a lot. «Wild axolotls ... are critically endangered because of drained, polluted water and introduced fish.» The clues are drained water, pollution and new fish, and the writer is saying the axolotl could die out.
fact: Endanger means to put someone or something in danger, or to make harm likely.
fact: An «endangered species» is an animal or plant that might die out.
fact: Endanger is a verb: endangers, endangered, endangering.
fact: «Many Hawaiian honeycreepers are endangered because mosquitoes spread bird malaria.»
fact: «American alligators recovered from being endangered once hunting was controlled.»
exercise: «Running by the pool can endanger others.» What does endanger mean here? | To help others swim faster | To make others laugh | To cool others down | *To put others in danger
exercise: «Many hammerheads are endangered by fishing.» What does endangered mean here? | Very happy and free | Newly born | *Likely to die out | Found only in lakes
exercise: Which word is NOT a form of the verb endanger? | endangers | endangering | endangered | *dangerous
test: «Wild axolotls are critically endangered because of drained, polluted water.» What might happen to axolotls if their water keeps being polluted? | They will grow much longer | They will be found in more lakes | *They might die out | They will learn to swim faster
test: A school poster says, «Running near roads can endanger children.» What does endanger mean? | Teach children to cross roads | Give children a free lunch | *Put children at risk of harm | Make children feel sleepy
exam: Which sentence uses endanger correctly? | *Littering can endanger animals that eat plastic | Littering can endanger the colour blue | Littering can endanger a happy birthday | Littering can endanger a good night's sleep
